cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Nursing Consistency Index (NCI): Data and Code"
message: >-
  If you use this dataset or code, please cite both the article and this
  repository.
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Tajima
    given-names: Hiroyuki
    affiliation: "Faculty of Nursing, Shumei University, Japan"
abstract: >-
  Data, analysis scripts, and figure-generation code for an information-
  theoretic audit of three commercial large language models (GPT-4o, Claude
  Opus 4.5, Gemini 2.5 Flash-Lite) on 30 nursing clinical scenarios across
  four sampling temperatures. The Nursing Consistency Index (NCI) is defined
  as 1 - H(R) / log2(k), where H(R) is the Shannon entropy of the empirical
  response distribution and k is the number of options.
keywords:
  - nursing education
  - large language models
  - reliability
  - Shannon entropy
  - clinical decision support
  - reproducibility
